GCC PR target/88343: r31 is saved in every PIC function on Darwin

powerpc-darwin sets up the picbase in r31 only when a function really
needs it, but decides whether to *save* r31 on nothing more than
-fPIC - and -fPIC is the Darwin default. So every function gets

	stw r31,-4(r1)
	...
	lwz r31,-4(r1)

whether or not it ever touches r31. In a WebKit build that is about
19% of all functions: two instructions, a stack store and a load that
misses on a cold frame, in the prologue and epilogue of sixteen
thousand functions.

Iain Sandoe reported this in December 2018 and it was fixed for GCC
7.5 and 8.3 - "it's possibly required for 6.x if someone is
maintaining a branch there, they might wish to apply it." Nobody did.
We are, so here it is.

This is the form that shipped in 7.5 (Alan Modra's rework, r268722),
not the first attempt: the original fix was reverted on both branches
because it under-saved r30 for 32-bit soft-float ABI_V4 Linux and
miscompiled glibc. That failure was entirely on the V4 side and cannot
reach a Darwin-only cross compiler, but the later form is the one
upstream settled on, so it is the one to carry.

The dead #if TARGET_MACHO block in first_reg_to_save goes with it, as
upstream removed it in the same commit: it tested exactly the
predicate that rs6000_reg_live_or_pic_offset_p now tests.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
@@ -24107,8 +24107,25 @@
 	      || get_pool_size ()))
 	return true;
 
-      if ((DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_V4 || DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_DARWIN)
-	  && flag_pic)
+      /* When calling eh_return, we must return true for all the cases
+	 where conditional_register_usage marks the PIC offset reg
+	 call used or fixed.  */
+      if (crtl->calls_eh_return
+	  && ((DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_V4 && flag_pic)
+	      || (DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_DARWIN && flag_pic)))
+	return true;
+
+      if (DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_V4
+	  && (flag_pic == 1 || (flag_pic && TARGET_SECURE_PLT))
+	  && df_regs_ever_live_p (RS6000_PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM))
+	return true;
+
+      /* Darwin sets up the picbase only when it is really used, so
+	 saving r31 for any -fPIC function saves it in the ~19% of
+	 functions that never touch it.  Test the same predicate the
+	 prologue does.  (GCC PR target/88343, fixed in 7.5 and 8.3.)  */
+      if (DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_DARWIN
+	  && flag_pic && crtl->uses_pic_offset_table)
 	return true;
     }
 
@@ -24139,13 +24156,6 @@
       && rs6000_reg_live_or_pic_offset_p (RS6000_PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM))
     first_reg = RS6000_PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM;
 
-#if TARGET_MACHO
-  if (flag_pic
-      && crtl->uses_pic_offset_table
-      && first_reg > RS6000_PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM)
-    return RS6000_PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM;
-#endif
-
   return first_reg;
 }
 
